E('captain cook|james cook', 'Captain James Cook was a British navigator and explorer.', 'He lived from 1728 to 1779.', 'He made three great voyages across the Pacific.', 'He mapped New Zealand and the east coast of Australia.', 'He crossed the Antarctic Circle.', 'He was killed in Hawaii in 1779.', 'His voyages opened the way to British colonisation, with lasting harm to Indigenous peoples.')
E('lewis and clark', 'Lewis and Clark led the first US expedition across the American West to the Pacific.', 'The journey lasted from 1804 to 1806.', 'President Jefferson sent Meriwether Lewis and William Clark after the Louisiana Purchase.', 'A Shoshone woman, Sacagawea, guided and interpreted for them.', 'They mapped land and recorded hundreds of new species.', 'They reached the Pacific coast in November 1805.')
E('roald amundsen|amundsen|south pole', 'Roald Amundsen was a Norwegian explorer who led the first expedition to reach the South Pole.', 'He reached it on 14 December 1911.', 'He beat Robert Falcon Scott’s British team by about five weeks.', 'He used dogs and skis expertly.', 'Scott and his companions died on their return journey.', 'Amundsen also first sailed the Northwest Passage.')
E('ernest shackleton|shackleton|endurance', 'Ernest Shackleton was an Anglo-Irish Antarctic explorer.', 'His Endurance expedition lasted from 1914 to 1917.', 'His ship, Endurance, was crushed by sea ice.', 'He led his men across ice and open sea to safety.', 'He sailed a small boat 1,300 kilometres to South Georgia for help.', 'Remarkably, all his men survived.', 'The wreck of Endurance was found in 2022.')
E('ibn battuta', 'Ibn Battuta was a Moroccan scholar and one of history’s greatest travellers.', 'He lived from 1304 to about 1369.', 'He travelled for nearly 30 years.', 'He visited Africa, the Middle East, India, Central Asia and China.', 'He covered about 117,000 kilometres, far more than Marco Polo.', 'His account is called the Rihla.')
E('zheng he', 'Zheng He was a Chinese admiral who led huge naval expeditions.', 'His voyages took place from 1405 to 1433.', 'He served the Ming dynasty.', 'His fleets had hundreds of ships, some enormous.', 'He sailed to South-East Asia, India, Arabia and East Africa.', 'China later ended the voyages and turned inward.')
E('amelia earhart|earhart', 'Amelia Earhart was an American aviation pioneer.', 'She lived from 1897 to 1937 (presumed).', 'In 1932 she became the first woman to fly solo across the Atlantic.', 'She disappeared over the Pacific in 1937 while trying to fly around the world.', 'Her fate is still a mystery.', 'She inspired generations of women in aviation.')
E('charles lindbergh|lindbergh', 'Charles Lindbergh was an American aviator.', 'He lived from 1902 to 1974.', 'In 1927 he made the first solo non-stop flight across the Atlantic.', 'His plane was called the Spirit of St. Louis.', 'The flight took about 33.5 hours.', 'His baby son’s kidnapping in 1932 was a notorious crime.')
E('jacques cousteau|cousteau', 'Jacques Cousteau was a French ocean explorer and filmmaker.', 'He lived from 1910 to 1997.', 'He co-invented the Aqua-Lung, an early scuba device, in 1943.', 'His films and TV shows revealed the underwater world.', 'He sailed his ship, Calypso, around the world.', 'He became a passionate conservationist.')
E('muhammad ali|cassius clay', 'Muhammad Ali was an American boxer, often called the greatest of all time.', 'He lived from 1942 to 2016.', 'He was born Cassius Clay.', 'He won Olympic gold in 1960 and was heavyweight champion three times.', 'He said he would “float like a butterfly, sting like a bee”.', 'He refused to fight in Vietnam and was stripped of his title.', 'His fights included the “Rumble in the Jungle” and “Thrilla in Manila”.')
E('pele|pelé', 'Pelé was a Brazilian footballer, one of the greatest of all time.', 'He lived from 1940 to 2022.', 'He won three World Cups, in 1958, 1962 and 1970.', 'He scored over 1,000 goals in his career, by his count.', 'He was 17 when he won his first World Cup.', 'He was known as “O Rei”, the King.')
E('jesse owens', 'Jesse Owens was an American track and field athlete.', 'He lived from 1913 to 1980.', 'He won four gold medals at the 1936 Berlin Olympics.', 'His victories challenged Nazi ideas of racial superiority.', 'He faced racism at home despite his success.')
E('michael jordan', 'Michael Jordan is an American basketball player, widely seen as the greatest.', 'He was born in 1963.', 'He won six NBA championships with the Chicago Bulls.', 'He won two Olympic gold medals.', 'His Air Jordan shoes became a global brand.')
E('usain bolt', 'Usain Bolt is a Jamaican sprinter, the fastest man ever recorded.', 'He was born in 1986.', 'He set the 100-metre world record of 9.58 seconds in 2009.', 'He won eight Olympic gold medals.', 'His “lightning bolt” pose became famous.')
E('serena williams', 'Serena Williams is an American tennis player, one of the greatest ever.', 'She was born in 1981.', 'She won 23 Grand Slam singles titles.', 'She won one while pregnant, in 2017.', 'She and her sister Venus dominated women’s tennis.')
E('lionel messi|messi', 'Lionel Messi is an Argentine footballer, one of the greatest of all time.', 'He was born in 1987.', 'He spent most of his career at Barcelona.', 'He has won a record eight Ballon d’Or awards.', 'He led Argentina to win the 2022 World Cup.')
E('cristiano ronaldo|ronaldo', 'Cristiano Ronaldo is a Portuguese footballer.', 'He was born in 1985.', 'He has played for Manchester United, Real Madrid and Juventus.', 'He is the all-time top scorer in men’s international football.', 'He has won five Ballon d’Or awards.')
E('world cup|fifa world cup', 'The FIFA World Cup is the world’s biggest football tournament.', 'The first was held in Uruguay in 1930.', 'It is held every four years.', 'Brazil has won it five times, the most.', 'Uruguay won the first one.', 'Billions of people watch it.')
E('babe ruth', 'Babe Ruth was an American baseball player.', 'He lived from 1895 to 1948.', 'He played mainly for the New York Yankees.', 'He hit 714 home runs, a record for decades.', 'He was called “the Sultan of Swat”.')
E('wimbledon', 'Wimbledon is the oldest tennis tournament in the world.', 'It was first held in 1877.', 'It is played on grass in London.', 'Players must wear mostly white.', 'Strawberries and cream are a tradition there.')
E('tour de france', 'The Tour de France is the world’s most famous cycling race.', 'It was first held in 1903.', 'It lasts about three weeks.', 'The leader wears the yellow jersey.', 'It ends in Paris.')
